      "content": "Definition: Understandability refers to how easily developers can comprehend and maintain the test code.\n\nTask: Improve the understandability of the test `TestGeohashUtils_testHashLenToWidth.java` (path:- /Users/tenghaha/Projects/New_Agent_understandability_improvement/data/original/spatial4j/manual/testcases/TestGeohashUtils/TestGeohashUtils_testHashLenToWidth.java). The refactored code must be syntactically correct and compilable against the provided CUT signatures. Do not alter the runtime behaviour of the original test: the same methods must be called with the same arguments and produce the same expected outcomes.\n"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "I'll read both the original test and the CUT to understand the code before improving it.Now I'll write the improved test with better understandability — clearer variable names, named constants for array indices, a named delta, and descriptive assertion messages.The improved test compiled successfully. The refactored version replaces cryptic array-index literals with named constants (`LAT_HEIGHT_IDX`, `LON_WIDTH_IDX`), names the tolerance `DELTA`, renames `boxOdd`/`boxEven` to `oddLenDimensions`/`evenLenDimensions`, adds descriptive assertion messages, removes unused imports and the unused `ctx` field, and adds a Javadoc comment explaining the odd/even cell-shape invariant — all without changing any method calls, arguments, or expected values."
    }
